{"id":"5fc287ea-9e0b-41ad-b5b1-58ddcb6d4e5b","object":"chat.completion","created":1784982978,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"```json\n{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"capacity\\\" not in case or \\\"trials\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must contain 'capacity' and 'trials'\\\")\\n    capacity = case[\\\"capacity\\\"]\\n    trials = case[\\\"trials\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(capacity, int) or capacity < 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"capacity must be a non-negative integer\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(trials, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"trials must be a list\\\")\\n    for t in trials:\\n        if not isinstance(t, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each trial must be a dict\\\")\\n        if \\\"signature\\\" not in t or \\\"reflection\\\" not in t or \\\"success\\\" not in t:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each trial must have 'signature', 'reflection', 'success'\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(t[\\\"signature\\\"], str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"signature must be a string\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(t[\\\"reflection\\\"], str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"reflection must be a string\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(t[\\\"success\\\"], bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"success must be a boolean\\\")\\n\\n    memory = []\\n    for idx, trial in enumerate(trials):\\n        sig = trial[\\\"signature\\\"]\\n        refl = trial[\\\"reflection\\\"]\\n        succ = trial[\\\"success\\\"]\\n\\n        # Deduplication: only for failure trials, update existing entry with same signature\\n        if not succ:\\n            # Look for an existing entry with the same signature\\n            found = False\\n            for entry in memory:\\n                if entry[\\\"signature\\\"] == sig:\\n                    entry[\\\"last_trial\\\"] = idx\\n                    entry[\\\"reflection\\\"] = refl\\n                    entry[\\\"success\\\"] = False\\n                    found = True\\n                    break\\n            if not found:\\n                memory.append({\\n                    \\\"last_trial\\\": idx,\\n                    \\\"reflection\\\": refl,\\n                    \\\"signature\\\": sig,\\n                    \\\"success\\\": False\\n                })\\n        else:\\n            # Success trials always add a new entry (no dedup)\\n            memory.append({\\n                \\\"last_trial\\\": idx,\\n                \\\"reflection\\\": refl,\\n                \\\"signature\\\": sig,\\n                \\\"success\\\": True\\n            })\\n\\n        # Trim if over capacity\\n        if len(memory) > capacity:\\n            # Sort by priority: failures first, then recency descending, then signature lexicographic\\n            memory.sort(key=lambda e: (e[\\\"success\\\"], -e[\\\"last_trial\\\"], e[\\\"signature\\\"]))\\n            # Keep first 'capacity' entries\\n            memory = memory[:capacity]\\n            # Restore chronological order (ascending last_trial)\\n            memory.sort(key=lambda e: e[\\\"last_trial\\\"])\\n\\n    # After all trials, ensure capacity (though trimming after each insertion guarantees it)\\n    if len(memory) > capacity:\\n        memory.sort(key=lambda e: (e[\\\"success\\\"], -e[\\\"last_trial\\\"], e[\\\"signature\\\"]))\\n        memory = memory[:capacity]\\n        memory.sort(key=lambda e: e[\\\"last_trial\\\"])\\n\\n    # Extract signatures in the same order as memory\\n    signatures = [entry[\\\"signature\\\"] for entry in memory]\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"memory\\\": memory,\\n        \\\"signatures\\\": signatures\\n    }\\n\"\n}\n```","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python function `solve(case)` that implements a specific reflection memory update. The case p